✅ Ansible Roles: Rules & Regulations (Important Points for Notes)
1. Fixed Directory Structure
Roles me har folder ka naam predefined hota hai.
Ansible sirf inhi folders ko recognize karta hai:
	roles/
	└── <role_name>/
	    ├── tasks/          → Tasks (main.yml mandatory)
	    ├── handlers/       → Handlers (main.yml)
	    ├── vars/           → Variables (main.yml)
	    ├── defaults/       → Default variables (main.yml)
	    ├── files/          → Static files (for copy module)
	    ├── templates/      → Jinja2 templates (.j2)
	    └── meta/           → Role metadata (dependencies, etc.)

2. main.yml is Mandatory
Har folder (tasks, handlers, vars, etc.) ke andar main.yml hona chahiye.
Agar main.yml nahi hoga, Ansible us folder ko ignore kar dega.
3. No hosts in Role Files
Role ke tasks/main.yml me hosts: nahi likh sakte.
hosts sirf playbook me hota hai.
	❌ Galat:
		# tasks/main.yml
		- hosts: node1   # ← NOT ALLOWED in role
		  tasks:
    			- ...
	✅ Sahi:
		# tasks/main.yml
		- name: install httpd
		  yum:
		    name: httpd
		    state: present
